title: `|| true` on the pytest step of a composite action
origin: issue #213 A1. A composite action's steps run inside the job that calls it, and its definition was not ci: v0.6.0 passes this with zero findings (beneath `test/`, #217's overlay reads it as a test file). The same line in a workflow blocks
=== before: .github/actions/test/action.yml ===
name: test
description: run the test suite
runs:
  using: composite
  steps:
    - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
      with:
        python-version: "3.12"
    - run: pip install -e .[test]
      shell: bash
    - run: pytest
      shell: bash
=== after: .github/actions/test/action.yml ===
name: test
description: run the test suite
runs:
